# SAEA-BENCH-cacheorder-q4km — the combined cache bench: slot affinity +
# stable-first prompt order + evidence-sized timeout (owner GO 2026-08-11
# "land the V1 patch and the combined bench" (translated from Chinese)).
#
# Supersedes SAEA-BENCH-idslot-q4km, whose read-out (ABORTED, 95 calls,
# 1 cache hit in 91 evidence slices) proved pinning alone cannot help while
# the per-slice rolling tail sits in the system message AHEAD of the stable
# evidence block — the cacheable prefix dies before the evidence starts. The
# one hit re-prefilled exactly tail+audio (~799 tok): every link of the chain
# works the moment the prefix is stable.
#
# Fragment q4km-cacheorder, three deltas vs locked config A (same server args):
#   id_slot "per-sample"                  — sample→slot pinning (already built);
#   prompt_order "evidence-first-system-v2" — [system: evidence…, instruction+tail]
#                                           [user: audio]; bare-core requests are
#                                           byte-identical under both orders;
#   timeout_seconds 240 → 420             — the armed logging finally named the
#                                           silent killer: a runaway evidence
#                                           slice decoding toward the 1024-token
#                                           cap at ~3 tok/s needs ~340 s and hit
#                                           the 240 s ceiling deterministically
#                                           (TimeoutError ×2 → skip ×2 → abort);
#                                           420 s makes the retry able to flag it
#                                           as saturation instead of dying.
#
# OFF reference: SAEA-E-002F-r4-matched attempt d02706 (42.7 min, WER 0.2513).
# Pre-registered predictions: prefill per slice drops to ~900 tok after each
# sample's first slice; wall 15-25% below the reference; WER inside the
# same-config noise band [0.2359, 0.2680] + digit/entity spot-check — note the
# order change IS a semantic prompt change, so the WER equivalence read is a
# real scientific check, not a formality. Adoption: all three → re-lock as the
# deployment config before the R4 n=10 re-run; any miss → analyze which delta
# failed before retiring anything.
#
